ern lunar programme were quantified by LRO instruments. A scout mission that became the foundation of the modern lunar era.",[504,508,511,515],{"met":53,"label":505,"note":506,"type":507},"LAUNCH","Atlas V 401 from Cape Canaveral SLC-41 (carried LCROSS impactor as secondary).","nominal",{"met":12,"label":509,"note":510,"type":507},"LOI","Lunar orbit insertion 2009-06-23.",{"met":45,"label":512,"note":513,"type":514},"PRIME MISSION","1-year exploration phase (NASA programme) begins.","info",{"met":516,"label":517,"note":518,"type":514},455,"EXTENDED SCIENCE","Mission extended to multi-year science phase under NASA SMD.","/orrery/images/missions/lro/03.webp"],"uses":{"params":["id"]}}]}
